{
  "date": "2026-10-13",
  "problem": "Screenshot overlay stays active after divider release; zoom stops despite live source responses.",
  "causes": [
    "A dispatched fitted-width guard could never match a newer viewport, withholding the completion required to dispatch the queued replacement.",
    "A resize notification marked JS active without any dispatched request; a native no-op had no terminal acknowledgement.",
    "Pinned Tinymist reconnect registered the same renderer again; the single-document selector rejected it while source updates continued.",
    "Unavailable, disposed, reset or replaced renderers could silently discard accepted native work before its final acknowledgement."
  ],
  "fixes": [
    "Sharp readiness compares cached fitted geometry with the CURRENT live container width, rather than the obsolete request width; native serial completion retains the raster while dispatching queued work.",
    "Only an accepted native request establishes JS ownership.",
    "Renderer registration deduplicates identical implementations and remains bounded; distinct implementations remain ambiguous.",
    "Versioned rejection/abandonment releases exactly the failed request, retires capture and waits for fresh renderer readiness. Paint/input callbacks verify renderer identity and exact ownership. Rejection never echoes an unversioned abort."
  ],
